{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:42:31.345809Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0942Z-0b72", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-003", "target": "C-598727de", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is not satisfied as it stands because no test exercises its scenario. The only two-tenant check in the admin route tests is the list half of it: in the test of accounts carrying roles and teams, tenant B's admin zed lists users and sees only zed. No test has B's admin read or patch one of A's users, grant a role to A's service account, list A's user's IdP links, or post a team with a forged tenantId, and none asserts afterwards that tenant A's rows are unchanged. The production code looks right (the tenant comes from the session through requireAdminContext, getAccount and listIdpLinks run under the caller's tenant, and the team body schema has additionalProperties false), so the fix is a new Node test over the server that traces the scenario; the project's security checklist requires every tenant-scoped query to be covered by a two-tenant test and the design promises each route a two-tenant scenario. WHEN tenant A holds humans ann and bob and a service account, tenant B h", "text_sha256": "fc0ad82e72ad950377b31f107016100e8f5b8f6e944dbde1c21fdcd22ded9256", "answer_sha256": "42b6b277634285978b0f746e2d47152eaf2f6c01d19544723996e7798bb8f08e", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:42:31.347074Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0942Z-0b72", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-96e47324", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The criterion is satisfied. The registry in src/api/error-codes.ts holds exactly the 22 entries of the scenario with the statuses and messages given, and the named test asserts the scenario in full: it compares the sorted key set of ERROR_CODES with its 22 expected keys, deep-compares status and message of every entry, checks isRegisteredCode true for each of the 22 and false for cursor_invalid, the empty string and NOT_A_CODE. The key-set comparison alone would fail against the 16-entry registry of the base, so the test discriminates; the harness has no red record only because the task changed this frozen test in place, as the design records. The stale title (16 codes) is required by the task and does not affect what the test asserts.", "text_sha256": "8955218be2f8f9508dd06b129dbdf9990af927812860e61a717269ef7dd8147d", "answer_sha256": "6f987711d2dcd75dbeb6652c1adc3a3f23848dd2417fc8451845499ed132c1a0", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:42:31.355220Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0942Z-0b72", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 9, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-005", "target": "F-cde045de", "decision": "reject", "by": "agent", "reason": "the same gap as Q-003 and Q-006: no test covers C-598727de, so the admin routes have no test of tenant isolation (tenant B requests at tenant A ids, a forged tenantId in a team body, tenant A rows unchanged). The fix is one new test over the server that traces C-598727de.", "text_sha256": "b928dd657a6e9c47a905426c1a2fb55dba07e9935350e0678292e8e2412d6961", "answer_sha256": "f4b44ea6bbe83b61f5e365e8383023656fa66842362f01af8b5bbafb446621a3", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:42:31.355954Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0942Z-0b72", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 10, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-006", "target": "F-28a40cf9", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding stands: the criterion is not covered by any test. The only two-tenant checks in the admin route tests are list calls by tenant B's admin zed, who lists users, teams, roles and group mappings and sees only tenant B's rows. No test has B's admin read or patch one of tenant A's users, grant a role to A's service account, list an A user's IdP links, or post a team whose body carries a forged tenantId, and no test asserts afterwards that tenant A's rows are unchanged. The production code appears correct, since every handler takes the tenant from the session through requireAdminContext and the body schemas refuse additional properties, so the fix is a new Node test over the server that traces the scenario; the project's security checklist requires every tenant-scoped query to be covered by a two-tenant test and the design promises each route a two-tenant scenario. WHEN tenant A holds humans ann and bob and a service account, tenant B holds human zed, and B's tenant admin sends GE", "text_sha256": "1407efb783404f1ec5b331394c631d61338250815f525727142687def1a3b97c", "answer_sha256": "8bd79af936d1ec96b7f97a29f9c500cc145d405310f9b0303ecfe938d4c7e908", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-10-31T09:42:31.356990Z", "run_id": "r-20261031T0942Z-0b72", "unit": "openspec:add-admin-api", "seq": 11, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-007", "target": "F-c28b995d", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding is waived: the criterion is satisfied and the named test asserts its whole scenario. The registry in src/api/error-codes.ts holds exactly the 22 entries the scenario lists, each with the status and message given. The test compares the sorted key set of ERROR_CODES with its 22 expected keys, deep-compares status and message of every entry, checks isRegisteredCode true for each of the 22 and false for cursor_invalid, the empty string and NOT_A_CODE. The key-set comparison would fail against the base's 16-entry registry, so the test discriminates. The gate reports no discriminating test only because the task changed this frozen test in place rather than adding a new one, which the design records as the chosen approach; the stale title naming 16 codes is required by that in-place change and does not affect the assertions.", "text_sha256": "6146dc840bd278510d9a4390ca1ebe6113f17a0d6191d2d71ecc71265fae8650", "answer_sha256": "a5bfe02b43e11b3ae15f2cfa2c46bfc9b7bd73052a97cfc90d7b72915878cda4", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
